    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "We mapped the area around the projected intersection of the Las Vegas Shear Zone and the Lake Mead Fault System in order to establish the nature of slip along these faults and the distribution and age relationships of the associated structures.The field data indicate at least two stages of structural development and the structures formed during the last stage are consistent with a mechanical model that assumes a NS-directed regional compression since mid-to late-Miocene.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
